WEBVTT

00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:04.701
[FOOTSTEPS SLOSHING]

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.703
Oh, come on.

00:00:06.703 --> 00:00:09.121
[GRUNTING]

00:00:09.121 --> 00:00:11.249
[MUFFLED MUTTERING]

00:00:12.291 --> 00:00:13.919
♪ Where the city sleeps ♪

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:18.006
♪ And I'm the only one And I walk alone ♪

00:00:18.006 --> 00:00:20.425
[GROANS]

00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:23.386
♪ I walk alone I walk alone ♪

00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:25.263
Of course you'd be singing that song.

00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:27.849
I can sing something else if you like.

00:00:27.849 --> 00:00:29.100
Suit yourself.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.603
♪ Sometimes I wish ♪

00:00:31.603 --> 00:00:34.981
♪ Someone out there Will find me ♪

00:00:34.981 --> 00:00:41.905
♪ Till then I walk alone ♪ Mm?

00:00:41.905 --> 00:00:44.991
[SQUIRREL VOCALIZING "BOULEVARD OF BROKEN DREAMS"]

00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:46.284
[GRUNTS]

00:00:51.163 --> 00:00:52.916
What you looking at, son?

00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:55.501
Never seen anyone steal something before?

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.545
You some kind of goody-goody?

00:00:57.545 --> 00:00:59.255
I'm no goody-goody.

00:00:59.255 --> 00:01:01.340
In fact, apparently, I'm bad.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.010
Yeah, I've made some mistakes, which is what I thought

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.388
kids are supposed to do, right? Learn, grow, evolve.

00:01:07.388 --> 00:01:10.558
But I guess, for this rabbit, the die is cast.

00:01:10.558 --> 00:01:12.936
And you know what? I don't care anymore.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:14.646
Oh, good for you, son.

00:01:14.646 --> 00:01:16.856
But if I can just suggest one thing,

00:01:16.856 --> 00:01:19.651
next time you meet a grizzled old thief on the street,

00:01:19.651 --> 00:01:21.611
maybe don't open up so much.

00:01:21.611 --> 00:01:24.322
Sorry. No, I like it.

00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:26.240
It's just, out here, not everyone's

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.868
as emotionally evolved as I am. Ah.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.496
Name's Barnabas. Nice to meet you.

00:01:31.496 --> 00:01:33.623
Peter. Take a peach.

00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:38.294
You said you weren't a goody-goody.

00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:40.880
No. I'm no goody-goody.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.382
I'm a baddy-baddy.

00:01:43.382 --> 00:01:46.177
[GRUNTING SOFTLY]

00:01:46.177 --> 00:01:48.972
SHOPKEEPER: Oy! Oh, no.

00:01:48.972 --> 00:01:51.057
Come on. I've had it with you rats!

00:01:51.057 --> 00:01:52.725
I hate when they call us rodents.

00:01:52.725 --> 00:01:54.769
Come back here! PETER: And when they try

00:01:54.769 --> 00:01:57.229
and hit us with a broom. That is not what a broom is for!

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:58.773
SHOPKEEPER: Get out of my shop!

00:01:58.773 --> 00:02:01.359
[YELLS] [GRUNTS]

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:02.986
Oh, I've had it with you rats!

00:02:02.986 --> 00:02:03.987
[GROANS]

00:02:03.987 --> 00:02:05.613
You owe me a peach, son.

00:02:05.613 --> 00:02:07.740
Lucky I had this safe house nearby.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.660
Where you from? None of your business, old man.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.911
What?

00:02:11.911 --> 00:02:14.664
Uh, well, you told me not to open up.

00:02:14.664 --> 00:02:16.166
Ha, now you're learning,

00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:19.293
but, uh, also, I am genuinely curious.

00:02:19.293 --> 00:02:22.421
I'm from the country, on a farm, near a pond.

00:02:22.421 --> 00:02:25.216
Really? Where'd you get that jacket?

00:02:25.216 --> 00:02:27.760
It looks just like one my old friend used to have.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.012
It was my dad's.

00:02:29.012 --> 00:02:30.722
[MAILMAN WHISTLING] [SHUSHING]

00:02:33.058 --> 00:02:34.976
We got to go.

00:02:34.976 --> 00:02:35.894
[RABBITS GRUNTING]

00:02:35.894 --> 00:02:38.104
[♪♪♪]

00:02:40.523 --> 00:02:42.483
Oof!

00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:43.609
You okay, son?

00:02:43.609 --> 00:02:44.610
Yeah. I'm fine.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.987
[CLICKS TONGUE]

00:02:45.987 --> 00:02:47.488
Did you just wink at me?

00:02:47.488 --> 00:02:49.824
Oh, um, sorry. No, no.

00:02:49.824 --> 00:02:51.951
The only other rabbit I knew who could wink

00:02:51.951 --> 00:02:55.580
was my friend from the country, and he lived next to a pond.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.417
Wait a minute. That farmer, his name isn't McGregor, is it?

00:02:59.417 --> 00:03:02.921
Yeah. Are you Peter Rabbit?

00:03:02.921 --> 00:03:05.715
Yeah. I can't believe it.

00:03:05.715 --> 00:03:06.925
My old friend,

00:03:06.925 --> 00:03:09.094
I think he was your dad. Oh!

00:03:09.094 --> 00:03:11.012
MAILMAN: They're in the recycling bin!

00:03:11.012 --> 00:03:13.973
Ah! What do we do? We have some fun.

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:16.434
[♪♪♪]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.978
SHOPKEEPER: There you are! MAILMAN: Ugh!

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:21.647
How is this fun? Because they actually believe

00:03:21.647 --> 00:03:25.026
they have a chance. Okay.

00:03:25.026 --> 00:03:27.361
[LAUGHING] [BLOWS RASPBERRY]

00:03:27.361 --> 00:03:29.989
♪ Yeah, I came to play Hey, hey ♪

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:33.492
♪ Get the competition Out the way ♪

00:03:33.492 --> 00:03:34.744
[PETER LAUGHING]

00:03:35.828 --> 00:03:37.914
Should this be in paper or plastic?

00:03:37.914 --> 00:03:39.749
No one really knows.

00:03:39.749 --> 00:03:41.709
♪ I just can't Control it tonight ♪

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:43.878
♪ My feet go from left To the right ♪

00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:45.797
♪ I just can't Control it tonight ♪

00:03:45.797 --> 00:03:47.673
♪ My feet go from left To the right ♪

00:03:47.673 --> 00:03:49.759
♪ My lips keep on going Up and down, hey... ♪

00:03:49.759 --> 00:03:52.511
[LAUGHS, GROANING]

00:03:52.511 --> 00:03:54.806
SHOPKEEPER: Got you! Aah!

00:03:57.142 --> 00:03:58.517
What do we do now?

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.437
[GROANING]

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:05.024
[GRUNTS]

00:04:06.025 --> 00:04:08.027
[CHUCKLES]

00:04:08.027 --> 00:04:10.029
[GASPS, SHOUTS]

00:04:12.531 --> 00:04:15.076
You're right! That was fun. Yeah.

00:04:15.076 --> 00:04:18.537
And there's a lot more of that around every corner.

00:04:18.537 --> 00:04:19.872
[PETER CHUCKLES]

00:04:19.872 --> 00:04:20.999
MAN: Got you!

00:04:20.999 --> 00:04:23.375
[♪♪♪]

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:24.418
Now, come on.

00:04:24.418 --> 00:04:26.420
Get in there, rabbit.

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:28.506
[♪♪♪]

00:04:33.343 --> 00:04:35.763
Who are these people? Where are they taking us?

00:04:35.763 --> 00:04:37.307
Stay calm, son.

00:04:37.307 --> 00:04:39.349
I won't let anything happen to you.

00:04:39.349 --> 00:04:40.810
[PANTING]

00:04:41.769 --> 00:04:43.813
NIGEL: And here.

00:04:43.813 --> 00:04:45.148
And there.

00:04:45.148 --> 00:04:46.316
Mm-hm. Here.

00:04:47.441 --> 00:04:49.277
And that's a fingerprint.

00:04:50.987 --> 00:04:52.738
I just need to say something.

00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:54.240
My book is very personal to me,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.492
and I don't want it to be compromised.

00:04:56.492 --> 00:04:58.953
I'd be spinning in my grave if it was ever adapted

00:04:58.953 --> 00:05:03.875
into some sassy hip-fest, purely for commercial gain,

00:05:03.875 --> 00:05:06.127
probably by an American.

00:05:06.127 --> 00:05:07.170
Mm-hm.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.629
I give you my word

00:05:08.629 --> 00:05:10.589
that I will be your ferocious guardian,

00:05:10.589 --> 00:05:12.466
a fortress between your art

00:05:12.466 --> 00:05:15.553
and all who wish to boorishly capitalize on it.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.515
Let's do it. Ha-ha! Hurrah!

00:05:19.515 --> 00:05:22.727
ALL: Hurrah! Hurrah! Hurrah!

00:05:22.727 --> 00:05:24.645
I'm telling you, this guy's garbage.

00:05:24.645 --> 00:05:27.106
Of course, making it more contemporary

00:05:27.106 --> 00:05:28.607
would increase the readership

00:05:28.607 --> 00:05:30.318
and benefit your preservation fund

00:05:30.318 --> 00:05:32.987
by, say, putting the rabbits in high-tops and T-shirts?

00:05:32.987 --> 00:05:34.404
ALL: Huh?

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:40.119
But you're a purist. I respect that.

00:05:40.119 --> 00:05:42.621
Sir, Marvin Stuart's outside for you.

00:05:42.621 --> 00:05:44.414
Ah, Marvin.

00:05:44.414 --> 00:05:45.666
One of our authors.

00:05:45.666 --> 00:05:47.377
[WHISPERS] Marvin Stuart.

00:05:47.377 --> 00:05:50.046
Hi, Marvin. I'll be right down.

00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:52.173
We bought him that car when his book hit number one.

00:05:52.173 --> 00:05:53.383
BEA & THOMAS: Mm.

00:05:53.383 --> 00:05:55.218
Marvin made a picture book

00:05:55.218 --> 00:05:56.510
about butterflies.

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.304
Gorgeous, elegant.

00:05:58.304 --> 00:06:01.974
You could hang it in a museum. Sold 250 copies.

00:06:01.974 --> 00:06:03.684
I made a small suggestion.

00:06:04.643 --> 00:06:07.521
Sold 15 million copies.

00:06:08.398 --> 00:06:11.276
That's more than Dickens.

00:06:11.276 --> 00:06:14.153
Where's Peter? I'm starting to get worried.

00:06:14.153 --> 00:06:16.406
This is not like him. The last time I saw him,

00:06:16.406 --> 00:06:18.324
we were staring at the billboard.

00:06:18.324 --> 00:06:22.120
ALL: Ah, the billboard.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.955
But seriously, where is Peter?

00:06:23.955 --> 00:06:26.165
[♪♪♪]

00:06:29.001 --> 00:06:31.170
[SHOP BELL JINGLES]

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:33.256
You got two this time. Nice one.

00:06:37.802 --> 00:06:39.762
MOTHER: Well, I don't know why I'm here.

00:06:39.762 --> 00:06:41.806
Ah! I want that one.

00:06:41.806 --> 00:06:45.351
He's just like Peter from that book Nana gave me.

